SDG 13: Climate Action
Introduction
Project Background
Climate change is one of the most urgent global challenges today. The United Nations Sustainable Development Goal 13 calls for immediate action to reduce greenhouse gas emissions, enhance climate awareness, and promote sustainable lifestyles across all sectors of society.
Universities play a critical role in educating and engaging young people in climate action. Although many students are interested in environmental protection and sustainability, they often lack practical, user-friendly tools to monitor their daily carbon footprint.
Environmental awareness alone cannot easily translate into real low-carbon behavior, because students cannot visualize or track the environmental impact of their daily activities such as commuting, dining, and resource consumption on campus.
Furthermore, most campuses do not provide a dedicated digital platform for students to record, calculate, and reflect on their carbon emissions. Campus sustainability teams also lack structured data to understand student behavior and improve campus-wide environmental initiatives.
To fill this gap, our project proposes a campus-focused application called Campus Climate Action.
Project Purpose
This project aims to design and develop a lightweight software prototype that helps students track their daily carbon footprint, participate in low-carbon activities, and build sustainable habits. At the same time, the project allows team members to practice professional 
software engineering skills using the Agile Scrum methodology in a real-world development process.
Project Scope
This is a 4 week prototype development project that includes requirement analysis, system design, interactive prototype development, functional testing, and project reporting. The project does not include full server deployment, large-scale user release, or long-term maintenance.
The focus is on demonstrating how software engineering can support SDG 13 Climate Action at the university level.

Project Objectives
Product Objectives
- Develop a functional prototype named Campus Climate Action for university students.
- Allow students to log daily activities, calculate personal carbon emissions, and view visual reports.
- Provide personalized low-carbon suggestions, low-carbon challenges, check‑in functions, and a reward system.
- Include basic climate education content to increase environmental awareness.
- Support simple campus-level data collection for sustainability management.
Learning Objectives
- Apply the complete SDLC in practice.
- Understand and implement Agile and Scrum project management.
- Gain experience in team collaboration using Trello and GitHub.
- Develop skills in UML modeling, UI/UX prototype design, system testing, and project documentation.
Expected Outcomes
- A usable interactive prototype with core carbon-tracking functions.
- Complete project documentation including research, design, testing, and Agile process records.
- Successful project delivery within the 4‑week timeline.
- A formal presentation and full project report.

