Project Methodology
Agile Software Development
The project uses the Agile development approach, which supports iterative, flexible, and user-centered development. Compared with the Waterfall model, 
Agile allows the team to adjust functions, respond to feedback, and improve the system continuously during development.
This is highly suitable for a short‑term student project with evolving requirements.
Scrum Framework
The team uses Scrum to structure the development process:
- Product Backlog: List of all requirements and features.
- Sprint Backlog: Tasks selected for each sprint.
- Sprint: Fixed‑length development cycle.
- Sprint Review: Evaluate completed work at the end of each sprint.
- Sprint Retrospective: Reflect on teamwork and process improvement.
Collaboration Tools
- Trello: Task management and sprint progress tracking.
- GitHub: Version control, document storage, and submission.
- Figma: UI design and prototype development.
- Office tools: Report writing and presentation preparation.

Project Timeline & Sprint Plan (4 Weeks)
The project is divided into Pre‑Sprint, Sprint 1, Sprint 2, and Final Sprint.
