- Goals: Finalize roles, complete SDG research, define product vision, set up tools.
Key Tasks:
- Assign team roles and responsibilities.
- Complete SDG 13 research report.
- Create User Stories and Product Backlog.
- Set up Trello board and GitHub repository.
- Deliverables: Research report, Product Vision, User Stories, Backlog, tool setup.
Sprint 1 – Week 2: Design & Early Prototype
- Sprint Goal: Complete requirement analysis, UML modeling, UI design, and core prototype framework.
Key Tasks:
- Draw Use Case and Class Diagrams.
- Design UI sketches for main pages.
- Build basic prototype structure.
- Develop carbon emission calculation logic.
- Create test plan.
- Deliverables: UML diagrams, UI sketches, early prototype, test plan.
Sprint 2 – Week 3: Development & Testing
- Sprint Goal: Complete interactive functions, implement rewards and suggestions, perform testing.
Key Tasks:
- Finish carbon calculation and report visualization.
- Develop personalized suggestions and check‑in features.
- Optimize UI and interaction.
- Conduct functional testing and bug fixing.
- Update Burndown Chart.
- Deliverables: Full interactive prototype, test report, Burndown Chart.
Final Sprint – Week 4: Finalization & Presentation
- Goals: Final optimization, full documentation, presentation, submission.
Key Tasks:
- Fix remaining bugs.
- Collect all Agile artifacts and project documents.
- Prepare presentation slides and rehearse.
- Complete and submit the full project report.
- Deliverables: Final prototype, complete report, presentation, full records.

System Functional Requirements
The system includes five core modules:
Carbon Footprint Calculation
- Record commuting, dining, and campus activities.
- Automatically compute carbon emissions.Visualization & Reporting
- Show data through charts and dashboards.
Personalized Low‑Carbon Recommendations
- Provide customized advice to reduce emissions.
Low‑Carbon Challenges & Reward System
- Support check‑ins and reward points to encourage participation.
Climate Education Content
- Deliver articles and tips about SDG 13 and sustainability.
The system follows three principles: lightweight operation, campus‑oriented functions, and motivational design.

Project Risk Management
- Requirement instability: Freeze core functions after planning; only adjust minor features.
- Task delays: Monitor progress via Trello and Burndown Chart; adjust tasks early.
- Prototype defects: Complete test plan early; perform two rounds of testing.
- Team communication issues: Clear role division; regular team meetings; standardized submission rules.

